Z||000005||Jackalrr||11-25-2000||05:53 PM||||I ended up having to scrape mine out with a knife. It was in there pretty good. <P>After you put the new one in with the glue or silicone make SURE to put the sun roof back on while it dries or it will not fit right and you will have a leak.||||reg||1
Z||000006||BAM-BAM||11-25-2000||11:54 PM||||  Thanks Jackl, I'll do that. I just pulled the old one out today. I had to do a little scraping and while I was at it I went ahead and refinished the inner rail, came out nice.<BR> What adhesive did you use? Oh and also, I drilled those 1/4 inch holes in the bottoms of all 4 corners. That should help me out some. I also replaced my sunroof hardware. I guess I have all bases covered. Let me know on the adhesive.<P>  Peace, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000007||Jackalrr||11-26-2000||01:17 PM||||I used silicone, but mine still doesn't fit right. I am pretty sure that it is because I did not put the sun roof back on for a day or two and it just dried the wrong way. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||robertjay||11-26-2000||05:55 PM||||I'd pobably use a good windshield urethane.  Get the stuff with the half million year shelf life, my brother swears by it on any window or weatherstrip sealing.||||reg||1
